{"name": "Cryodrakon", "clade": "azhdarchidae", "isd": false, "isnote": "", "sum": "Giant azhdarchid from the late Campanian Dinosaur Park Formation of Alberta, Canada — long referred to Quetzalcoatlus.", "ws": [5, 10], "wsnote": "The holotype (immature) indicates at least 5 m; a large referred neck vertebra suggests about 10 m for mature individuals.", "holotype": "TMP 1992.83 — Dinosaur Park Formation, Dinosaur Provincial Park, Alberta.", "material": "Associated, disarticulated partial skeleton without skull: 4th cervical, rib, humerus, pteroid, 4th metacarpal, tibia, metatarsal; referred material from many individuals.", "completeness": "partial", "exceptional": "Holotype bones bear bite marks and an embedded tooth tip, probably from Saurornitholestes.", "biology": "Lived inland on a coastal plain; like other azhdarchids, probably a terrestrial stalker of small animals.", "author": "Hone et al. 2019", "fad": 83.6, "lad": 72.2, "early": "Campanian", "late": "", "type_species": "Cryodrakon boreas", "pbdb_occ": 2, "species": [{"name": "Cryodrakon boreas", "author": "Hone et al. 2019", "fad": 83.6, "lad": 72.2, "interval": "Campanian", "ref": "D. W. E. Hone, M. B. Habib, and F. Therrien. 2019. Cryodrakon boreas, gen. et sp. nov., a Late Cretaceous Canadian azhdarchid pterosaur. Journal of Vertebrate Paleontology 39(3):e1649681"}], "formations": [{"ids": ["dinosaur-park-canada"], "formation": "Dinosaur Park", "group": "Belly River", "members": [], "country": "Canada", "regions": ["Alberta"], "interval": "Late Campanian", "n": 2, "ma": [72.2, 83.6]}], "images": [{"kind": "life", "file": "Cryodrakon_boreas.png", "src": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Cryodrakon_boreas.png/960px-Cryodrakon_boreas.png", "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cryodrakon_boreas.png", "artist": "Connor Ashbridge", "license": "CC BY 4.0", "licurl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0", "date": "2025-03-22", "caption": "Life reconstruction of Cryodr